// 0.0.6 T05: an enum-variant pattern in `choose` must fail the compile
// loudly. `Foo(x)` names a variant of no enum, and the scrutinee is an
// `int`, so typeck rejects it with `EnumPatternMismatch` (T05) instead of
// the T02-era "unsupported feature" placeholder — the whole pipeline must
// reject it instead of silently miscompiling (the old placeholder returned
// from the function before printing "B").
func main() {
    print("A");
    r = choose 1 { when Foo(x) { 111 } otherwise { 222 } };
    print("B");
}
